WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
You're building a mobile app.

2
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.400
You drop in the exact CSS that flawlessly handles your web layouts,

3
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.000
expecting everything to snap into place.

4
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:13.000
Instead, you're met with immediate crashes over invalid units

5
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.000
or child elements that stack vertically and disappear

6
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.000
because the engine doesn't recognize your web first ro logic.

7
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:24.000
The breakdown happens because React Native doesn't use a web browser rendering engine.

8
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.000
It isn't reading CSS at all.

9
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.000
This diagram shows the difference.

10
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.000
On the left is the sprawling complexity of the web document object model.

11
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.000
On the right is React Native's actual rendering core,

12
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.000
the yoga layout framework.

13
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Yoga is a highly constrained mobile optimized emulation of standard flex box.

14
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.000
To style successfully on mobile, you have to map the exact points

15
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:49.000
where yoga diverges from standard web behavior.

16
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:53.000
That means adjusting to three constraints, strict syntax rules,

17
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:56.000
single-value flex shorthand, and modern build tools.

18
00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:01.000
Understanding yoga's mechanical rules is the only reliable way

19
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:06.000
to bypass constant debugging and write predictable mobile interfaces.

20
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:11.000
The translation from web to mobile begins with how layout properties are formatted.

21
00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:15.000
This diagram demonstrates the first absolute rule of yoga.

22
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:19.000
When parsing a standard CSS property like background color,

23
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:24.000
the engine strips out the hyphen and forces strict camel case syntax.

24
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:29.000
In addition, CSS units like pixels or REMs are entirely invalid,

25
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.000
leaving only a bare integer.

26
00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:34.000
These bare numbers represent density independent pixels.

27
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:37.000
The engine automatically scales that constant integer

28
00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:41.000
to match the physical pixel density of the user's specific hardware.

29
00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:46.000
Beyond syntax, the core mechanics of how elements align on the screen also change.

30
00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:50.000
Standard web flex box automatically aligns child elements horizontally,

31
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.000
defaulting to a row orientation.

32
00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:56.000
Instead, react native completely switches this default.

33
00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:00.000
All layouts inside the yoga engine initialize as a vertical column.

34
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.000
This override exists because mobile screens are physically constrained

35
00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:06.000
to a portrait-first orientation.

36
00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:12.000
These foundational shifts in syntax and orientation show that physical mobile constraints

37
00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:16.000
dictate react native's logic over established web conventions.

38
00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:21.000
The largest source of layout errors for web developers comes from a single property,

39
00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.000
the flex shorthand.

40
00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:28.000
In standard CSS, the flex property accepts up to three distinct values in a string,

41
00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:33.000
controlling how an element grows, shrinks, and sets its base size.

42
00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.000
The react engine rejects this.

43
00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:39.000
The react native flex prop accepts exactly one number.

44
00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:42.000
Here is how the engine handles a positive integer.

45
00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:47.000
An input of flex one mechanically expands into flex grow one,

46
00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:50.000
flex shrink one, and a flex basis of zero.

47
00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:54.000
Practically, this commands an element to expand evenly,

48
00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.000
perfectly filling the available space.

49
00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:00.000
When the input changes to zero, the output channels instantly adjust to zero

50
00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:04.000
for grow and shrink and set the basis to auto.

51
00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:08.000
In this state, the element will not expand or compress to fill space.

52
00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:12.000
It is rigidly locked to its explicit width and height properties.

53
00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:16.000
Finally, an input of negative one yields a zero for grow,

54
00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:19.000
a one for shrink, and an auto basis.

55
00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:23.000
Attempting to pass a multi-value string like flex one one auto

56
00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:26.000
will completely crash the layout engine.

57
00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:30.000
If the standard single number combinations don't meet your design needs,

58
00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:35.000
you must write out the grow, shrink, and basis properties explicitly on separate lines.

59
00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:39.000
Yoga drops the flexibility of CSS shorthand syntax

60
00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:43.000
to ensure predictable constrained memory allocation on mobile hardware.

61
00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:46.000
Moving past internal flex box logic,

62
00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:50.000
cross-platform rendering introduces another layer of discrepancies,

63
00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.000
starting with shadows.

64
00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:56.000
Under the legacy architecture, casting a shadow meant writing fragmented code,

65
00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:01.000
specific shadow properties for iOS, and a separate elevation property for Android.

66
00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:07.000
React Native 0.76 and its new architecture unified this fragmentation,

67
00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:14.000
introducing a single CSS compatible box shadow property that works across both platforms.

68
00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:18.000
Other style properties maintain architectural quirks.

69
00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:22.000
The transform property, for example, requires an array of specific objects,

70
00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:25.000
not a continuous text string.

71
00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:30.000
To bypass these exact quirks, many developers turn to utility frameworks like native wind.

72
00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:35.000
Native wind acts as a compiler, translating familiar tailwind CSS classes

73
00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:39.000
directly into yoga compatible native objects at build time.

74
00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:45.000
But upgrading to native wind version 4 introduces a specific configuration risk,

75
00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:49.000
where styles fail to apply despite a successful build.

76
00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:53.000
Version 4 strictly demands that you use a babble preset in your configuration,

77
00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:55.000
rather than a babble plugin.

78
00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:59.000
If you use the old plugin method, the app compiles without errors,

79
00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:04.000
but styles never render because the compiler skips processing the utility classes.

80
00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:10.000
Furthermore, native wind version 4 is incredibly incompatible with tailwind CSS version 4.

81
00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:15.000
You must explicitly pin your project dependencies to the tailwind 3.x range,

82
00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:18.000
or the integration will fail to apply your styles.

83
00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:24.000
Injecting web based utility tools into a react native environment requires precise synchronization

84
00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:26.000
between your bundler and compiler.

85
00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:30.000
Modern architecture brings powerful web light convenience to mobile development,

86
00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:34.000
but only if you execute the build step configuration with absolute precision.

87
00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:37.000
Let's look at the complete functioning ecosystem.

88
00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:40.000
This diagram outlines the entire pipeline.

89
00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:44.000
Utility classes and styling objects pass through strict compilers,

90
00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:48.000
transforming into constraints that lock into the yoga engine below.

91
00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:52.000
During translation, hyphens convert to camel case, units are stripped,

92
00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:54.000
and flux values compress to single numbers.

93
00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:57.000
You must design your layouts anticipating this system,

94
00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:59.000
building for columns before rows.

95
00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:03.000
Treating a mobile application exactly like a web browser,

96
00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:06.000
guarantees technical debt, and endless debugging.

97
00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:12.000
These deviations from web CSS provide the mechanical efficiency required for fluid mobile performance.

98
00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:16.000
By respecting the strict boundaries of the yoga engine

99
00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:18.000
and maintaining precise build configurations,

100
00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:23.000
you can execute complex styling for robust, predictable mobile interfaces.

